[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a basic checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html:19[39m:

  - A native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m wrapped in a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the text toggles it. On/off state is the
    browser's own — no JS.
  - One CSS rule strikes through and greys the label when checked, so "done" is visible.

  To add more tasks, copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">…</label>[39m block and change the text. I used a placeholder item ("Write
  the task list") since the page had no items yet — swap in real ones or drop it if you're rendering items from
  elsewhere.

  Not committed. Not run in a browser — verify visually if you want confirmation.

